# Bench run artefacts are generated measurements, not source. The format:check
# glob covers bench/**/*.{js,json} so the harness is gated; without this line a
# single local run would put machine-written JSON in front of the formatter.
bench/runs

# The same rule for the recordings committed as replay fixtures, kept as a safety
# net. Since #261 neither tool reaches them: lint-staged matches src/**, bench/**
# and root-level files only, and format:check uses the same three globs, so
# nothing under tests/** is currently in scope. The entry matters the day one of
# those globs widens, because the fixtures must stay byte-exact — Prettier
# rewrites `"points": [\n 9989\n]` as `"points": [9989]`, and the byte-for-byte
# assertion in tests/main/bench/replay.test.js would then compare a rebuild
# against a file the formatter edited.
tests/fixtures/bench
